  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Food Crisis Response in East Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed project in East Darfur aims to enhance the food security status of affected communities in Yassin and Adila localities through the provision of agricultural inputs, training and livestock support. The project will directly benefitnbsp18,125 individuals, including IDPs, refugees, and host communities. In Yassin and Adila localities, 3000 of the most vulnerable households will receive critical agricultural inputs and necessary training services to enhance crop production. This includes the distribution of improved seeds such as sorghum and millet for household consumption throughout the year as well as groundnuts for market sale. On the field crop trainings will be conducted, comprising five sessions covering technical cultivation practices, seed propagation, and climate adaptation. Furthermore, 350 vulnerable women heading households in these localities will receive five goats each along with necessary training and veterinary services. Animal husbandry training will be provided Additionally 50 Community Animal Health Workers (CAHWs) will receive refresher training to enhance their skills in vaccination, treatment, and community awareness. To promote peace and social cohesion,nbspthe facilitation and strengthening of Peace Committee will be supported in Yassin locality. The committee will undergo training in conflict resolution and peacebuilding techniques, enabling them to address conflicts, particularly those arising between farmers and animal breeders. Furthermore, the committee will develop and implement a community-based action plan to improve social cohesion and address underlying grievances related to land access and market issues.nbspltbrgtFor the proposed project WV Sudan will receive a match fund up to 15%, from other World Vision offices. Notwithstanding anythingnbspstated to the contrary in this Grant Agreement, World Vision Sudan,nbspWorld Vision Canada and World Vision United Kingdomnbspare all Partners as defined under this Grant Agreement, and each shall be jointly and severally liable for allnbspprogrammatic delivery, technical, administrative and financial requirements, quality assurance, timely and accurate reporting and any andnbspall other obligations of the Partner as stipulated in the Grant Agreement.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
